Z||000000||sk8rpunk48162||12-25-2000||08:59 PM||||  Hi i have a 1986 pontiac fiero se.  And i have no radio right now i had one but it stopped working and i thought it was the fuse, also i am going to get a cd player soon to put in and i looked at the fuse box and its missing the fuse for the radio it looks like it uses a big fuse because i tried to put in a regular fuse and it wouldnt fit it looks like it needs a big one,, could someone tell me which fuse to use?? A special type?? could somebody send me a pic of their fuse box thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-25-2000||10:14 PM||||I think what you are talking about is the 30 amp power accessory circut breaker.  I dont have a pic of mine right now, but it is much much bigger than a regular fuse.  They are silver and made out of metal.  If you dont have anything like this in your fuse box, go to your local auto parts store and ask for one.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-25-2000||11:11 PM||||The radio is powered by a 10 amp fuse marked radio and a 20 amp fuse marked Bat. These both the same format 2 blade plastic fuse. <P>the metal can(s) are 30 amp thermal circuit breakers that have nothing to do with the radio. These are the large openings between "HTR A/C" and "CTSY LID". These breakers are only present on cars with power windows, power locks, and/or rear defog.<P>There are new notes in my cave about the radio. They are in the interior area.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-25-2000).]||||reg||1
